stackcats programs vendored for integration testing
====================================================

the `.in` files in this directory are stack cats programs sourced verbatim
from the `examples/` directory of the upstream stack-cats repository:

  https://github.com/m-ender/stackcats
  commit reference: examples/ at HEAD of the upstream repo at the time
  these were copied (see internal/integrationtest/testdata/gems/stackcats/
  for the full upstream snapshot)

each `.in` is the corresponding `<name>.sks` from `examples/`, renamed so
the goruby esolang test harness (which globs `*.in`) picks them up. the
sibling `.expected` files were generated by running

  ruby internal/integrationtest/testdata/gems/stackcats/ruby/interpreter.rb \
       <fixture>.in </dev/null > <fixture>.expected

under MRI 2.6.10, so the harness verifies that goruby's evaluator
matches MRI's output byte-for-byte on real third-party ruby code.

`examples/infinite-loop.sks` is intentionally omitted -- it never
terminates, so there's no useful MRI baseline to compare against.

`examples/logic-gates/` (a sub-directory of 4-bit truth-table programs)
is also omitted; the harness globs a flat layout and adding them would
need a naming convention, which seemed like overkill for a smoke
suite.

